        ":question/id": "1b5f24a7-25be-5f91-9261-490e6919b435",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-130006",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ on $A?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ means that we need to multiply the third row of the matrix by $\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nMultiplying the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
